    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d501-a8">

                <pb facs="0595" n="575" sameAs="frus:frus1864p3/pg575"/>

                <head>[Enclosure No. 9.]</head>
                <p>Having met in conference the several ministers, and having well understood the
                    nature of their communication, our government has agreed to take upon itself the
                    settlement of the indemnity which should have been paid by Mowosi Daizen,
                    consequent upon the war which has taken place with your ships in Choshu.</p>
                <p>For your information we address you this communication in writing.</p>
                <p>With respect and esteem,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>MAKINO BIDZEN-NO-KAMI.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>His Excellency <hi rendition="#small-caps">Robert H. Pruyn</hi>, <hi
                            rendition="#italic">Minister Resident of the United States in Japan,
                            &amp;c., &amp;c., &amp;c.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
                <closer><dateline rendition="#float-left"><date calendar="japanese-nengō gregorian"
                            when="1864-10-07">Ninth months 7th day of the 1st year of Grenji, (7th
                            October, 1864.)</date></dateline></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
